BAJAJ PULSAR 125 -NEON DISC LED Booking for Ex-Showroom Price,"Maximum Power: 8.68 kW (11.8 PS) @ 8500 rpmEngine Capacity: 124.38 ccBrake Front: DiscTire Type: TubelessConsole Feature: Fully Digital Reverse Monochrome LCDBajaj Auto Limited provides a 5-year or 75,000 km warranty (whichever is earlier) for the first owner, covering manufacturing defects through authorized workshops. However, proprietary parts like tyres, tubes, and batteries must be claimed directly from their respective manufacturers. Items like shock absorbers and speedometers are subject to the original manufacturer's approval, and Bajaj is not liable for consequential losses or repair delays. All legal disputes are limited to Pune jurisdiction. To keep the warranty valid, owners must complete the first three free services without lapse and subsequent paid services every 5,000 km or 120 days. All maintenance must occur at authorized centers using Bajaj DTS-i 10000 engine oil (drained every 10k km, topped up at 5k km). Owners must also replace periodic parts like filters as scheduled and present the original Owners Manual for all claims; direct factory claims are not accepted.","₹91,250",4.5,15 Ratings & 7 Reviews,15 Ratings & 7 Reviews,8.68 kW (11.8 PS) @ 8500 rpm,124.38 cc,Disc,Tubeless,"Fully Digital Reverse Monochrome LCDBajaj Auto Limited provides a 5-year or 75,000 km warranty (whichever is earlier) for the first owner, covering manufacturing defects through authorized workshops. However, proprietary parts like tyres, tubes, and batteries must be claimed directly from their respective manufacturers. Items like shock absorbers and speedometers are subject to the original manufacturer's approval, and Bajaj is not liable for consequential losses or repair delays. All legal disputes are limited to Pune jurisdiction. To keep the warranty valid, owners must complete the first three free services without lapse and subsequent paid services every 5,000 km or 120 days. All maintenance must occur at authorized centers using Bajaj DTS-i 10000 engine oil (drained every 10k km, topped up at 5k km). Owners must also replace periodic parts like filters as scheduled and present the original Owners Manual for all claims; direct factory claims are not accepted.",,,,Bajaj,Motorcycle
